note right of DocumentDeletionPolicy
  Current status:
  - UML defines non-destructive business history rules.
  - Some controllers/managers can still physically remove draft or
    reference child rows where that is valid.
  - There is no single policy service/test suite that proves
    protected business records cannot be hard deleted.

  Required behavior:
  - Posted/canceled documents, payments, movements, reservations,
    OrderHistory and StatusHistory are append-only/read-only records.
  - Draft-only hard delete is allowed only for entities that have no
    posted movements, payments, status history or business impact.
  - Reference data uses status=inactive/deletedAt when it may appear
    in historical documents.
end note

note right of ReferenceArchivePolicy
  Reference data policy:
  - Product, Category, Unit, Warehouse, Customer, Supplier,
    ProductPrice and InventoryReason must remain readable.
  - Prefer inactive status for hiding from new operations.
  - Use deletedAt only as soft archive.
  - Do not break old snapshots, document links or reports.
end note

note bottom
  Suggested implementation order:

  1. Add a small policy service or manager methods for archive/delete checks.
  2. Wire admin delete/archive actions through that policy.
  3. Add tests that hard delete is blocked for:
     posted InventoryDocument, StockMovement, Payment,
     OrderHistory, StatusHistory and ProductionOrder with documents.
  4. Add tests that draft-only cleanup is still possible where allowed.
  5. Add UI messages explaining why a record was archived instead of removed.
end note

@enduml
